# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COMPETITION DATA AND EVERYTHING DERIVED FROM IT.
#
# The ANRF AISEHack 2.0 rules make the Competition Data "Competition Use only":
# it may not be transmitted, duplicated, published or redistributed to anyone
# not participating. That covers the raw SLCs and it covers processed copies of
# them, so `work/gamma0/` — 656 MB of calibrated, geocoded gamma-nought over the
# AOI — is squarely out. So are the intermediate farm tables, which carry
# per-plot centroids taken from the competition shapefile.
#
# The three tables in `outputs/` are safe and ARE published: they are this
# project's own model output and were checked to hold no coordinate column.
# See README.md for where a reader gets the data themselves.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data/
work/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment. `.venv` here is a --system-site-packages shell over Homebrew
# Python and is not portable to another machine even if it were committed;
# requirements.txt is the reproducible statement.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs. `pipeline_clean.log` is the shipped run that every number in the
# write-up is traced to, and `writeup_trace.txt` is the token-to-line mapping
# that proves it — both are committed. The rest are development scratch from
# individual sessions, and shipping several pipeline logs with nothing saying
# which is current is worse than shipping one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/*
!logs/pipeline_clean.log
!logs/writeup_trace.txt

# Session scratch, not part of the submission.
NEXT_SESSION.md
